"""dictate-live: F9 dictation that types as you talk, and turns conversations into meeting transcripts.

First press: start listening and show a floating box. Each time you pause, the phrase
goes through the accurate engine (Parakeet by default) and is typed into the window
where F9 was pressed; while another window is in front, phrases wait and go in when
you return. A fast whisper model shows the phrase being spoken in grey.
When a second voice speaks long enough (or the box's Meeting button is clicked), text
goes to transcripts/ with speaker labels instead. During calls the computer's sound
is transcribed too.
Second press: finish the last phrase, insert what is waiting (or save the meeting).

Everything runs locally. Design: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md; terms: docs/DOMAIN.md.
"""
import array
import collections
import configparser
import datetime
import difflib
import io
import json
import math
import os
import queue
import re
import signal
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
import urllib.request
import uuid
import wave

import gi

